  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></math> denote the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></mrow></msup></math> term in the expansion of <math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math> If the ratio <math><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>:</mo><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and the sum of the coefficients of the second and third term is <math><mn>36</mn><mo>,</mo></math> then the value of&nbsp;<math><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;is",
